The service also uses caching to improve performance by reducing the number of requests made to the external API. The cache is configured to use the `@Cacheable` annotation and is named "resourceCache".

Error handling is also implemented using a comprehensive approach that includes meaningful error messages and status codes for clients. When an error occurs, the service will attempt to recover gracefully by retrying the request or returning an error message.

The service is designed to be scalable and maintainable by using best practices such as clean code, clear documentation, and unit testing. It also includes error handling and retries for failed requests to the external API.

