To handle large-scale data ingestion efficiently, this code uses a configurable number of worker threads that can be adjusted based on system resources available. The `process_logs()` method also includes retry mechanisms for failed operations and fallback strategies to minimize data loss in case of partial uploads to the third-party cloud storage service.

To ensure robust error handling and optimize memory usage, this code includes detailed logs for debugging and comprehensive unit tests and stress tests to validate performance under realistic load conditions. The `LogProcessor` struct is also designed to scale horizontally by allowing seamless addition of more processing nodes, making it easy to add more resources as needed.']

