The function also includes a `pthread_mutex_t` lock for concurrency control, which is acquired before updating the shared key-value store. This ensures that multiple instances of the function can concurrently update the shared key-value store without race conditions or data inconsistencies. The function also provides comprehensive error reports, including timestamps, operation details, and success/failure metrics, using an integrated logging framework.

