Here is an example of how to implement a real-time, scalable web service that processes incoming customer reviews, extracting mentions of specific products, and returns a JSON response mapping product names to lists of review IDs:

1. First, we will create a RESTful API endpoint using Node.js and Express.js. This endpoint will handle requests from clients and return responses in JSON format.
```javascript
const express = require('express');
const app = express();
const port = 3000;

app.get('/reviews', (req, res) => {
  // Handle incoming reviews and extract mentions of specific products
  const reviews = req.body.reviews;
  const productNames = ['product1', 'product2'];
  const reviewIds = [];

  reviews.forEach((review) => {
    productNames.forEach((productName) => {
      if (review.text.includes(productName)) {
        reviewIds.push({
          id: review.id,
          text: review.text,
        });
      }
    });
  });

  // Return a JSON response with product names and their corresponding review IDs
  res.json({
    productNames: productNames,
    reviewIds: reviewIds,
  });
});
```
