void process_string(char *str) {
    int i = 0;
    while (str[i]) {
        if (isupper(str[i])) {
            str[i] = tolower(str[i]);
        }
        i++;
    }
}

This function takes a string as input and processes it by converting all uppercase letters to lowercase. It uses the `isupper` and `tolower` functions from `<ctype.h>` to perform this conversion. The function iterates through each character in the string using a while loop, checking if each character is an uppercase letter with the `isupper` function. If it is, it converts it to lowercase with the `tolower` function and assigns the result back to the same index in the string. The function returns void because it operates on the input string without creating a new variable to store the processed string.']

