To balance the number of worker threads per node and optimize performance without causing resource exhaustion or excessive latency, we will use dynamic scaling to adjust the number of worker threads and the number of nodes based on current load and available resources. This will ensure that the tool is resilient against node failures and automatically reassigns tasks to maintain consistency across distributed nodes.

To provide clear and informative feedback to users during processing, we will offer detailed logging for debugging purposes. Additionally, we will include real-time metrics for monitoring performance and identifying bottlenecks. Users will be able to specify custom data transformation rules for different log file types, enabling the tool to adapt to various data formats and structures without modifying the core processing logic.

