This code defines a module for managing a multi-resolution grid (MRG) that supports dynamic spatial data operations across various scales. It integrates with an external geospatial data service API, allowing for real-time updates and retrieval of spatial data. The module handles varying data resolution requirements by maintaining separate maps for different resolution levels, each containing the corresponding spatial data. It also employs mechanisms to handle efficient memory usage, minimizing potential memory leaks and optimizing cache utilization.

The code includes a `MrgManager` class that manages the MRG and provides methods for adding, removing, and querying spatial entities at different resolution levels. The class uses a mutex and condition variable for synchronizing access to the data map, ensuring seamless integration with existing GIS systems while maintaining data consistency and integrity.

The module also includes two threads to handle incoming spatial data from an external service and dynamic spatial data operations at different resolution levels. These threads are implemented using a `std::thread` and `std::future`, respectively, allowing for concurrent access from multiple threads and processes while ensuring data consistency and integrity.

The code prioritizes maintainability by adopting best practices in code organization, documentation, and testing, making it easy to extend and modify in the future.']

