The system uses a dynamic configuration structure to allow for real-time updates to allowed issuers, expiration thresholds, and scopes. The circuit breaker pattern has been implemented to manage failures in external token signing and time synchronization services. Latency monitoring has been enabled using distributed tracing, and logs have been integrated with a centralized logging service for easy analysis and visualization.

Token revocation lists have been implemented with support for bulk revocation and automatic revalidation. User data access tracking has been introduced to track and log user activity, and GDPR compliance mechanisms have been added to provide users with the ability to export their activity logs. System integration and dependencies have been ensured through robust error handling and fallback mechanisms, and performance optimization has been achieved through efficient data structures and algorithms.

Testing and maintenance have been implemented using comprehensive unit tests, integration tests, and performance tests, which provide a structured approach to testing and monitoring the system's functionality."]

