<?php

class UserDAO {
  private $db;

  public function __construct($db) {
    $this->db = $db;
  }

  public function updatePassword($user, $newPassword) {
    // Validate password strength and handle error conditions
    if (!$this->isValidPassword($newPassword)) {
      return false;
    }

    // Update user's password in database
    $stmt = $this->db->prepare('UPDATE users SET password = :password WHERE id = :id');
    $stmt->bindValue(':password', $newPassword);
    $stmt->bindValue(':id', $user['id']);
    $stmt->execute();

    return true;
  }

  private function isValidPassword($password) {
    // Check for minimum length, at least one uppercase and lowercase letter, one number, and one special character
    if (strlen($password) < 8) {
      return false;
    }

    $uppercase = preg_match('/[A-Z]/', $password);
    $lowercase = preg_match('/[a-z]/', $password);
    $number = preg_match('/\d/', $password);
    $specialCharacters = preg_match('/[^a-zA-Z\d]/', $password);

    if (!$uppercase || !$lowercase || !$number || !$specialCharacters) {
      return false;
    }

    return true;
  }
}
```
This code defines a `UserDAO` class that has an `__construct()` method to initialize the database connection, and an `updatePassword()` method to update a user's password in the database. The `isValidPassword()` method is used to validate the password strength by checking for a minimum length of 8 characters, at least one uppercase and lowercase letter, one number, and one special character. If any of these conditions are not met, the function returns false.

The `updatePassword()` method first validates the password using the `isValidPassword()` function before updating it in the database. The `UPDATE` statement is prepared with a parameterized query to prevent SQL injection attacks.

This implementation is secure because it uses prepared statements and parameterized queries to prevent SQL injection attacks, and it also uses regex to validate the password strength. It is efficient because it only updates the user's password in the database when the validation checks pass."]

