public class DataProcessor {
    private static final String KAFKA_TOPIC = "my-kafka-topic";
    private static final String LOGSTASH_HOST = "localhost:5044";
    private static final int MAX_CONCURRENCY = 16;
    private static final long TIMEOUT = TimeUnit.SECONDS.toMillis(30);

    private final KafkaConsumer<String, String> kafkaConsumer;
    private final JedisPool jedisPool;
    private final ExecutorService executorService;

    public DataProcessor() {
        // Set up Kafka consumer
        kafkaConsumer = new KafkaConsumer<>(KAFKA_TOPIC, StringDeserializer.class, StringDeserializer.class);

        // Set up Redis pool
        JedisPoolConfig config = new JedisPoolConfig();
        config.setMaxTotal(MAX_CONCURRENCY);
        jedisPool = new JedisPool(config, LOGSTASH_HOST);

        // Set up executor service for concurrency
        executorService = Executors.newFixedThreadPool(MAX_CONCURRENCY);
    }

    public void processData() {
        while (true) {
            ConsumerRecords<String, String> records = kafkaConsumer.poll(Duration.ofMillis(TIMEOUT));
            List<Future<Void>> futures = new ArrayList<>();

            // Process each record in parallel using executor service
            for (ConsumerRecord<String, String> record : records) {
                futures.add(executorService.submit(() -> processRecord(record)));
            }

            // Wait for all futures to complete
            futures.forEach(Future::join);
        }
    }

    private void processRecord(ConsumerRecord<String, String> record) {
        // Preprocess and filter the data as needed
        String preprocessedData = preprocessAndFilterData(record.value());

        // Transform the data as needed
        String transformedData = transformData(preprocessedData);

        // Store the data in Redis for later retrieval
        jedisPool.getResource().set("data-" + record.key(), transformedData);
    }

    private String preprocessAndFilterData(String data) {
        // Implement data preprocessing and filtering here
    }

    private String transformData(String data) {
        // Implement data transformation here
    }
}
```
This microservice uses Kafka as the primary source of streaming data, with custom log streams also supported. The data is processed in parallel using an executor service to maximize throughput and resource utilization. Redis is used for caching and storing preprocessed data for later retrieval. Dependency management, concurrency control, scalability, data storage and retrieval, error handling, monitoring and alerts, and CI/CD pipeline are all considered in the design.']

