After updating the document, it notifies other tenants that the document has been updated using the `NotificationService`. This allows for real-time updates and ensures that all tenants have access to the latest version of the document.

The `DocumentUpdateRequest` class is used to represent the request data sent in the HTTP POST request. The `Token`, `TenantId`, and `DocumentId` properties are used to authenticate the user and enforce access controls, while the `Content` property is used to update the document contents.

The `ErrorResponse` class is used to return error messages when there are issues updating the document. It contains a single string property named `Message`.

