The `verify_file` method takes a file path and expected hash as input, and computes the SHA-256 hash of the file content. It then compares the computed hash with the expected hash and raises an exception if they do not match. The `_compute_file_hash` method is used to compute the hash of the file content, while the `_fetch_file_metadata` and `_fetch_file_content` methods are used to fetch the metadata and content of the file from each cloud provider in parallel.

The `verify_differential_hash` method supports differential hashing by computing the difference between the actual hash and the expected hash, and then comparing it with the expected hash. It also tracks the progress of hash computation and sends alerts in case of discrepancies between expected and computed hashes. The `_integrate_with_logging_service` method is used to integrate with an external logging service to track hash computation progress and errors.

The system is designed to handle large files efficiently by using a thread pool to fetch file metadata and content in parallel, and by computing the differential hash in parallel across multiple cloud providers. It also includes rate limiting and quota management to prevent abuse while ensuring fair usage across all users. The system can be integrated with a third-party notification service to send alerts in case of discrepancies between expected and computed hashes, ensuring proactive monitoring and response.

