The `validate_file_integrity` method first checks if the file exists and can be read. If it cannot, it returns an error message. Otherwise, it computes the MD5 hash of the file in fixed-size chunks (using the `hashlib` library) to minimize memory usage. It then sends the computed hash value to the API for verification using the `requests` library.

