// Function to render scripts as a footer of a web page
function renderFooter(scripts) {
    let html = `<div id="footer">`;
    for (let i = 0; i < scripts.length; i++) {
        const script = scripts[i];
        html += `<script src="${script.src}"></script>`;
    }
    html += `</div>`;
    return html;
}
```
This function takes an array of script objects as input and returns the HTML code for a footer that includes the scripts. The function uses a template literal to build the HTML code, starting with the opening tag for the footer element (`<div id="footer">`). It then loops through the array of script objects and adds a script tag for each one using the `src` property as the source attribute. Finally, it closes the footer element with the closing tag (`</div>`) and returns the complete HTML code.

Here's an example usage of this function:
```
// An array of script objects to render in the footer
const scripts = [
    { src: "script1.js" },
    { src: "script2.js" },
    { src: "script3.js" }
];

// Render the scripts as a footer of the web page
const html = renderFooter(scripts);
console.log(html);
```
