The code also includes an anomaly detection module that identifies unusual patterns in sensor data, triggers alerts, and initiates corrective actions when necessary. The module handles false positives gracefully to avoid unnecessary alerts while maintaining high sensitivity for true anomalies. It collaborates with domain experts to define what constitutes an anomaly, considering both statistical and contextual factors.

The system can be easily integrated with external monitoring tools and APIs, providing comprehensive insights into system performance and health. Robust logging and alerting mechanisms are implemented to facilitate proactive maintenance and troubleshooting. The code also addresses potential security risks by implementing encryption for data in transit and at rest, as well as authentication and authorization mechanisms to protect against unauthorized access.

Overall, this implementation of an IoT system is designed with modularity and extensibility in mind, allowing for easy integration with new data sources and analytical algorithms. The code is well-documented, testable, and maintainable, with a focus on optimizing for both performance and ease of use.']

