The code block also defines two error handling mechanisms: one for handling database errors and one for handling OAuth authentication errors. When a database error occurs, the code logs the error message and throws a new `RuntimeException` with a descriptive message. When an OAuth authentication error occurs, the code logs a warning message and throws a new `RuntimeException` with a descriptive message.

The code block also defines two configuration settings: one for enabling caching and one for setting the cache duration. The `enableCaching` setting is set to `true` by default, which enables caching of frequently accessed user data. The `cacheDuration` setting is set to 30 minutes by default, which sets the expiration time of cached data.

Overall, this code block provides a robust and scalable implementation of a PHP microservice for managing user profiles using OAuth authentication and a relational database. It addresses several real-world engineering challenges, including system integration, performance optimization, concurrency and threading, error handling and recovery, scalability, security, configuration management, monitoring and logging, and testing.']

