2. Multi-Tier Caching Architecture:

The multi-tier caching architecture will use a combination of in-memory and disk-based caching mechanisms to optimize memory usage and reduce latency for read-heavy workloads. The system will dynamically adjust based on access patterns and system load, balancing memory and disk usage, and minimizing cache thrashing to achieve optimal hit rates and reduced latency.
```java
public class CachingSystem {
    private final InMemoryCache inMemoryCache = new InMemoryCache();
    private final DiskBasedCache diskBasedCache = new DiskBasedCache();

    public void cache(String key, String value) {
        // Cache logic
        if (inMemoryCache.containsKey(key)) {
            return;
        } else {
            diskBasedCache.put(key, value);
            inMemoryCache.put(key, value);
        }
    }

    public String get(String key) {
        // Cache logic
        if (inMemoryCache.containsKey(key)) {
            return inMemoryCache.get(key);
        } else {
            return diskBasedCache.get(key);
        }
    }
}
```
